<title>TURKEY: Earthquake damages homes in eastern Turkey.</title>
<headline>Earthquake damages homes in eastern Turkey.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>An earthquake measuring four on the Richter scale damaged dozens of houses in the eastern Turkish province of Erzurum on Sunday but there was no word of casualties, Anatolian news agency said.</p>
<p>Around 70 houses in the village of Koprukoy were damaged in the quake. The Turkish Red Crescent society was to send 100 tents to the area, the agency said.</p>
